ges are pitching in  that allows them to earn some extra  money  it's being financed by private investors  and the german government's  international climate initiative  the farmers get the seedlings directly  from fair ventures once they receive  training on how and where to plant them  today kaharap is visiting farmer pasihan  he's only been involved in the project  for a year but he's already planted  several hundred sengon trees  the sengon is very fast growing  around  five to six meters in 11 months this is  why we love this kind of trees so much  because you know the more they grow the  more nitrogen they put in the soil the  more fertilizes the soil and that it  allows the farmers to actually plant any  other things in his field  and yeah this is how fast  it's growing and then imagine  a million million of trees in central  kalimantan  was planted by the farmers here  to absorb the carbon  for the farmer it's not only about  providing a stable income for himself  and later his children  like in many parts of borneo floods are  a growing problem here  these days our village floods three to  four times a year  it used to only flood once a year  but it doesn't seem to matter anymore  what the season is we still get flooded  i think it's down to the impact of  mining  the forest has been cleared so the  ground doesn't absorb the water anymore  and when it rains heavily  everywhere just floods  planting more trees could help prevent  such damaging floods in the future  more than a million new trees have been  planted throughout the region so far  some of them will now be felled and sold  as timber while others are planted in  their place  the idea is to attract more business to  borneo to help the farmers  the timber industry in indonesia now  it's still very centralized in java  island right and then we try to convince  the industry to also  invest in kalimantan or what we're  trying to do is we try to connect the  farmers directly with the industry to  cut dow